  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The diagonal – long pass, return and a shot at speed",
  "description": "Four lines and a goalkeeper in one half: D and A in the corners by the goal, C and B along the boards out at the defender positions. C plays a long diagonal pass to A and runs into the slot. A plays it straight back into C's path, and C shoots first time. Then the same from the other side: B passes to D, runs in and gets the return.\n\nRotation: A goes to B, B to C, C to D and D to A.\n\nVariation: A starts with the ball and passes to C, who plays it straight back and then runs into the slot. A plays another one-touch pass, and C shoots first time. That makes two give-and-gos and asks even more of the passes. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The long pass should be hard and along the floor."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A: play the return to where the runner is going, not where they were."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Vary forehand, backhand and volley."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Stick on the floor on the way into the slot, and shoot first time."
    }
  ],
